1
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,760
Based on our seating,

2
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:37,520
we'll split into two teams.

3
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,160
The teams will take turns acting as

4
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,120
the Guessing Team and Observing Team.

5
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,360
For the Guessing Team,

6
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,720
three will act out in a relay,

7
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:45,800
and one will guess the word.

8
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,000
Each prompt is timed.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,120
A correct guess earns one point.

10
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,720
Among the three actors,

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,440
one is an undercover player

12
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,040
who only gets partial info on the prompt.

13
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,280
While the other team is guessing,

14
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:58,160
the Observing Team can call them out anytime.

15
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,920
A correct accusation earns two points,

16
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,360
while a wrong one loses two points.

17
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,320
If we guess wrong twice in a row,

18
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,920
even without them doing a thing,

19
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,160
we'll still lose.

20
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,280
Let me give you a word of advice:

21
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,040
don't try to show off.

22
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:09,880
Reel it in a bit.

23
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,040
I just saw in Officer Huang's eyes...

24
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,400
He's already weirdly excited.

25
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,080
Let's decide first

26
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,400
which team goes first.

27
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,560
Rock, paper, scissors! Come on.

28
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:22,640
Rock, paper, scissors!

29
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,680
Rock, paper, scissors!

30
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:23,960
Paper!

31
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,240
Losers go first!

32
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,640
You go first.

33
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:28,920
You go first.

34
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:29,800
Winners go first!

35
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,040
Winners go first!

36
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,560
So do winners go first or losers?

37
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:33,520
Let's settle it right now.

38
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:33,880
Come on.

39
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,280
Wait, don't...

40
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,720
And here I was trying to cheat!

41
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,360
Hurry up, you guys!

42
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:43,320
Let's go.

43
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,440
Who's going undercover?

44
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,320
I'll go undercover.

45
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,000
I'll do it.

46
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:48,400
Get out of here.

47
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,040
I'll be the undercover.

48
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,160
Playing it out in the open, huh?

49
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,880
I'll guess.

50
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:55,320
You guess.

51
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,560
And one of the three of us will be undercover.

52
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,800
You be the undercover.

53
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,840
Why don't you go undercover?

54
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,040
I'm terrible at keeping secrets.

55
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,360
Can't hide a thing.

56
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,720
I can't keep anything inside.

57
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:05,200
Then you do it.

58
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,720
Then go stand over there.

59
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:16,760
Seven characters.

60
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,320
First character.

61
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,320
Slap?

62
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:21,280
No.

63
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:21,520
Pat?

64
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:22,560
Hit?

65
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,520
Hit? Seven characters, hit?

66
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,760
Could it be Bing?

67
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,840
Maybe Bing only got the first character.

68
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,560
Which character?

69
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:33,560
Second character.

70
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,160
Open.

71
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,800
Parting dark clouds in the sky...

72
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,680
Part? Hit... sky?

73
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:45,960
What's this?

74
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,040
We know it's "hit", right?

75
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:54,920
Open!

76
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:56,200
Sky!

77
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,240
Window!

78
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,560
Open the skylight and speak plainly!

79
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,160
Correct!

80
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:00,600
Nice!

81
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:06,560
Next!

82
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,400
How many characters?

83
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,280
I...

84
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,280
Too abstract!

85
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,120
How many characters?

86
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,800
Four words.

87
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,120
Four words?

88
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,400
Why?

89
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:41,680
What?

90
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,480
Close enough.

91
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:44,760
What?

92
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,160
Why?

93
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:46,840
What?

94
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,600
When?

95
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,760
It's not in Chinese!

96
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,160
Pass!

97
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,240
You jump, I jump.

98
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,600
You two acted out completely different things.

99
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,120
You were just showing off.

100
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,200
It was completely meaningless.

101
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,520
It wasn't even Chinese.

102
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,080
Still, I'll take it.

103
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,760
Like, "you do this, and I do that."

104
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:32,320
Something like that.

105
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,640
"You do this, I do that."

106
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,080
"You..."

107
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:37,600
"...jump..."

108
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,800
"...you jump, I jump."

109
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,160
Then why didn't you...

110
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:45,080
...just gesture this and that...

111
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,040
...and be done with it?

112
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,720
Bing!

113
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,080
"Report!"

114
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,640
Bing.

115
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,440
Wang Anyu, why don't you speak up!

116
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,120
I already did!

117
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,280
I called Bing out first!

118
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,680
Congratulations!

119
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,240
Minus two points.

120
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,280
You lose two points!

121
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,640
Minus two points for guessing wrong!

122
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,160
Guess one more round.

123
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,120
Minus two points.

124
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,760
I told you it wasn't Bing!

125
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,520
You're the one who analyzed it!

126
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,040
Bing!

127
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,360
You were faking it just now!

128
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:34,720
Let's make a bet.

129
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:35,760
Wager the points from the next round...

130
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,320
...and take a gamble!

131
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:38,560
Do dignity points count?

132
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,440
Points don't count...

133
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,200
...dignity does!

134
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,440
How much is dignity worth to us anyway?

135
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,760
Are we wagering points or not?

136
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,160
She's the undercover.

137
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:50,560
She might...

138
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,680
She might have had "jump."

139
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,640
She had a "jump" there.

140
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,280
She had "jump."

141
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:55,520
No.

142
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:55,720
That's not right.

143
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,920
Her first gesture was "you."

144
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,720
But that's her routine every round.

145
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,720
Call her out!

146
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,640
I thought it was Jingyu at first, too.

147
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,560
Then I thought it was Churan.

148
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,400
There are only three people in total!

149
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,080
You've guessed all three!

150
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,440
If you ask me, it's Churan.

151
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,000
Jingyu.

152
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,680
I pick Jingyu.

153
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,080
Relieved now.

154
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:19,920
Totally relieved.

155
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:22,040
My mind is instantly settled.

156
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,640
Congratulations, you got it right!

157
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,040
Look at what the three of us chose.

158
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,320
I swear, I'm not lying...

159
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,720
...my first guess...

160
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,880
...was Jingyu.

161
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:35,880
No, really.

162
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,920
But deep down I was...

163
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,160
No...

164
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,960
I thought you guys made sense...

165
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,080
...but I actually wanted to guess Jingyu all along.

166
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,160
Churan...

167
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,640
...great acting!

168
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,800
You knew I was the undercover, right?

169
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,920
And you knew it was three or four English words.

170
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,400
Bing was there yelling, "Pass! Pass!"

171
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,920
Couldn't you act a bit further back?

172
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,480
I was trying to watch from here...

173
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,240
...and she kept moving forward.

174
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,520
I didn't dare turn my head...

175
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,240
...so I was just peeking from here.

176
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,920
Even peeking, I couldn't see anything.

177
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,000
She just kept pushing forward while acting!

178
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,840
How did you act it out?

179
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,120
I thought it was...

180
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:06,080
So I...

181
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,240
Still, you played really well.

182
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,760
If it were up to me...

183
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,000
...I'd have caught you in round one.

184
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,400
Next time, just speak your mind.

185
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,800
Don't just keep it to yourself.

186
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,360
You take a guess.

187
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:20,640
I can guess, too.

188
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,400
That's so many words.

189
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:31,960
Did they just give us an essay?

190
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:33,600
Go ahead and guess.

191
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,440
Interesting.

192
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,120
Eleven words.

193
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:40,720
The first word.

194
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,720
The first word is that...

195
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:43,560
Fly.

196
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:44,640
No.

197
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:44,920
Big.

198
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,680
The second word.

199
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,160
Words two and three.

200
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:53,560
Big.

201
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,360
Pray.

202
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:56,720
Put the three together.

203
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,560
The first word.

204
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,360
Big.

205
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,280
And then?

206
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:06,960
Right, the first word.

207
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,040
Then the second...

208
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:14,000
Go on.

209
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,720
"Report!" Huang Jingyu!

210
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,160
Are you sure?

211
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:19,800
Bet.

212
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,880
Bet.

213
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,440
Bet.

214
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,360
It's a bet!

215
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:22,640
Bet.

216
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,080
It's you.

217
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,640
Huang Jingyu.

218
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:26,400
It's you.

219
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,200
Reported!

220
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,320
Why report already?

221
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,040
Aren't you...

222
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,800
We're only in round one!

223
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:31,640
Right.

224
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,880
To stop you from scoring points.

225
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,720
It's definitely you.

226
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,720
Think about it again.

227
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:35,520
Right?

228
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:36,520
Right?

229
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:37,840
Officer Huang.

230
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:40,560
Come on.

231
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,760
Incorrect.

232
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,440
I told you so!

233
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:53,760
Why are you so reckless?

234
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,960
I told you before we started,

235
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:56,800
don't show off!

236
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:02,440
Didn't you shout "bet" too?

237
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,080
"Bet."

238
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,440
"Bet."

239
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,000
"Bet."

240
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,800
"It's a bet!"

241
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:05,960
"Bet."

242
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,200
When an avalanche happens,

243
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,440
no snowflake is innocent.

244
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,640
Just now we were all united,

245
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,560
how did it come to this now?

246
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,600
We were all a bit impulsive.

247
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,160
Go on.

248
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:19,960
Keep acting, guys.

249
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:20,840
Keep playing.

250
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:21,960
Edit that part out.

251
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:22,240
Cut it!

252
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:25,560
*Journey to the West*.

253
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,920
What Friar Sand often says to Tang Monk.

254
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,080
Master.

255
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,320
Who? The first word.

256
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:31,200
Big.

257
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,480
Eldest Senior Brother!

258
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,200
Why would he call Master "Eldest Senior Brother"?

259
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,200
I messed up!

260
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,400
"Report!"

261
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,080
Xiao Hu!

262
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,400
Betting dignity again?

263
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,080
Reported again!

264
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,560
It can only be Xiao Hu.

265
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:50,360
Why do I feel like it's Bing?

266
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,440
Impossible.

267
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,520
But he's pretty sharp too.

268
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,880
He can guess the 11-word phrase.

269
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,240
No.

270
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,080
Xiao Hu.

271
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,080
Are you sure?

272
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,800
Betting the dignity of four people!

273
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,280
Am I involved in this too?

274
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,920
Don't lump me in with him.

275
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:11,320
Our dignity isn't the same thing!

276
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,040
Confirmed.

277
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:13,800
Bet it all on me!

278
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:14,200
Xiao Hu.

279
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:15,800
Answer:

280
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,200
Incorrect.

281
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,280
I knew it was Bing.

282
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,080
Three people, and two got it wrong.

283
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,440
I'll give you guys another chance.

284
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,080
Guess one more time.

285
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,760
Which one of these two is it?

286
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,920
I'll leave this highlight moment to you, Xiao Bai.

287
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,080
Him.

288
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,200
Wang Anyu.

289
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,160
Let's play a four-point round with you.

290
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,800
Come on.

291
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,600
Here it comes.

292
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,120
That's the look!

293
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:01,880
There it is.

294
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,040
I told you to tone it down.

295
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:04,480
Tone it down.

296
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,080
You've got nothing.

297
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:06,720
